  <description>
    <original_author id="organisation">eduLIMS</original_author>
    <lifecycle_state>unmanaged</lifecycle_state>
    <other_details id="archetypes">openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.report-result.v1 1.1.0 (CKM 1013.1.1324); openEHR-EHR-OBSERVATION.laboratory_test_result.v1 1.2.8 (CKM 1013.1.2191); openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.laboratory_test_analyte.v1 1.2.3 (CKM 1013.1.2881); openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.specimen.v1 1.1.3 (CKM 1013.1.331); openEHR-EHR-CLUSTER.device.v1 1.1.6 (CKM 1013.1.17)</other_details>
    <other_details id="licence">Built from openEHR CKM archetypes, copyright openEHR Foundation, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/); this template is shared under the same licence.</other_details>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>en</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>Records a measurement of a practical laboratory session in education: the result of one analyser run on one or more sample IDs, with the analyser, the order (practical) and the result status.</purpose>
      <use>Written by eduLIMS for the Epoch 2 Excel upload and by FerroBRIDGE for the Afinion 2 HL7 v2 results. The sample ID is the specimen's laboratory specimen identifier, the well position its specimen label, the practical the requester order identifier, and the analyser the medical device.</use>
      <misuse>Not for clinical diagnosis or patient care. Never holds a name, student number or e-mail address in any element.</misuse>
    </details>
  </description>
